  "note": "P8-T2 single token source (Plan \u00a710 + theme-tokens-v1 contract). One source, two generated consumers: ui/themes/tokens.h (C++ uint32_t 0xAARRGGBB accessors \u2014 NO Skia include) and ui/tokens.css (--xr-* custom properties). Both are GENERATED (tools/tokens_gen.py, --check diff-clean); never hand-edit the outputs. 'critical-red' is RESERVED in data + validator: it is never themeable to a non-alarming color (a theme doc mapping critical-red to anything outside the canonical alarming family is refused). Per-theme values: the 'themes' map carries a FULL value set per built-in theme; v1 ships 'light' (the P7 browser-chrome baseline, values preserved); T3 adds Dark/HighContrast/System(+2 curated) into this same data. Fonts: family tokens reference SYSTEM font stacks only \u2014 the bundled-font list is EMPTY in v0 (locked decision: fonts are P30 territory). T3: built-ins Light/Dark/HighContrast + curated Dusk/Prairie; 'system' is a resolver (system_resolution data); curated themes pass the full audit with ZERO waivers; built-in waivers (if any) are exact data rows with reasons.",
  "reserved": {
    "critical-red": "reserved token: never themeable to a non-alarming color; the loader/validator refuses any theme whose critical-red deviates from the canonical alarming family without an in-data waiver"
  },
